1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,148
Alex has checked the library twice.

2
00:00:02,659 --> 00:00:05,898
His headphone case is missing, and his bus leaves soon.

3
00:00:06,223 --> 00:00:07,616
He tells the campus group.

4
00:00:07,732 --> 00:00:12,934
Elena replies that she is still nearby and suggests
checking whether someone has handed it in.

5
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:18,216
Ava then posts that she found a black headphone case in
Library Study Room Two.

6
00:00:18,913 --> 00:00:22,419
She says she has already brought it to Mira at the
library desk.

7
00:00:22,802 --> 00:00:24,416
Could it belong to someone here?

8
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:26,564
FindBack is monitoring the channel.

9
00:00:26,807 --> 00:00:35,422
It automatically answers inside Ava’s thread, thanking
her and reminding everyone to keep identifying marks
and contents out of the public conversation.

10
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:38,545
Alex answers, “That might be mine.”

11
00:00:39,358 --> 00:00:42,806
He was studying in that room, and his case is plain
black.

12
00:00:43,619 --> 00:00:47,590
He has a possible connection, but no distinguishing
detail yet.

13
00:00:48,194 --> 00:00:51,352
Then Noah adds that his own case is plain black too.

14
00:00:52,652 --> 00:00:54,544
“We should check more than the color.”

15
00:00:55,241 --> 00:01:00,999
His comment makes the problem concrete: a common
appearance cannot establish whose item this is.

16
00:01:02,114 --> 00:01:04,169
Alex follows with a fuller report.

17
00:01:04,447 --> 00:01:09,080
He lost a black headphone case in the library that
afternoon and wants help checking it.

18
00:01:10,032 --> 00:01:14,142
FindBack responds in the same thread with a link to his
private recovery chat.

19
00:01:14,954 --> 00:01:19,355
In the private chat, Intake says it is reading his
report and preparing a draft.

20
00:01:19,865 --> 00:01:24,196
The draft records the item, color, location, and his
description.

21
00:01:25,148 --> 00:01:27,691
Alex is asked to check what the agent understood.

22
00:01:28,201 --> 00:01:30,918
Alex confirms, “Yes, that’s right.”

23
00:01:31,615 --> 00:01:36,677
Intake asks what marks, contents, or accessories would
help identify his case.

24
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:39,835
The desk also gets an initial comparison.

25
00:01:40,438 --> 00:01:44,119
His report is confirmed; ownership still needs
evidence.

26
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:46,929
But Alex is worried about missing his bus.

27
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:48,693
“Can you just release it?”

28
00:01:49,018 --> 00:01:52,002
he asks, admitting he cannot remember the marks.

29
00:01:52,815 --> 00:01:56,983
Intake explains that color alone is not enough for Mira
to release a case.

30
00:01:57,308 --> 00:01:59,131
His request stays open.

31
00:01:59,943 --> 00:02:06,062
Now Alex remembers: a red thread on the zipper, and the
initials R K on the inside label.

32
00:02:07,176 --> 00:02:12,911
Intake saves his exact words as his assertion and tells
him a fresh comparison is being prepared.

33
00:02:13,515 --> 00:02:18,321
The Matcher announces it is comparing Alex’s
description with the desk’s two black cases.

34
00:02:18,925 --> 00:02:21,119
Then the updated comparison arrives.

35
00:02:21,816 --> 00:02:26,088
His red thread and initials match the staff
observations for case B.

36
00:02:27,203 --> 00:02:29,420
It’s a possible match for Mira to judge.

37
00:02:29,664 --> 00:02:35,318
Mira approves case B for Alex, saying she checked both
details against the desk’s observations.

38
00:02:35,702 --> 00:02:38,569
Her decision stays in that exact comparison thread.

39
00:02:39,266 --> 00:02:43,248
FindBack reserves the case and privately tells Alex
that Mira approved it.

40
00:02:44,363 --> 00:02:50,446
Next, Mira sends collection instructions: ask for her
at the library desk and show the private recovery chat.

41
00:02:51,050 --> 00:02:53,685
FindBack delivers those instructions to Alex.

42
00:02:54,196 --> 00:02:57,853
Collection is arranged; handover and receipt are still
pending.
